{"name":"E. Honda Beige","hex":"#f8d77f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closed loop or eyelet at one end of a lariat or lasso, through which the other end of the rope is passed to form a much larger loop.","A grommet or other device intended to strengthen or otherwise improve a simple rope honda."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honda"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"E. Honda","blocks":[{"text":"Edmond Honda , better known as E. Honda, is a character created by Capcom for the Street Fighter fighting game series. Introduced in Street Fighter II as part of the starting lineup, he has appeared in Street Fighter Alpha 3, Street Fighter IV and the Capcom vs. SNK series, and made several cameos. Honda is a professional sumo wrestler and sentō proprietor. He is one of the original eight playable characters in Street Fighter II, representing Japan alongside Ryu."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Edmondhonda.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._Honda","wikidata":"Q2300080"},{"title":"Honda","blocks":[{"text":"Honda Motor Co., Ltd., commonly known as Honda, is a Japanese multinational conglomerate automotive manufacturer headquartered at the Toranomon Alcea Tower in Toranomon, Minato, Tokyo, Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Toranomon_Alcea_Tower_26Dec2025.jpg/330px-Toranomon_Alcea_Tower_26Dec2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honda","wikidata":"Q9584"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Honda_hq.jpg/500px-Honda_hq.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Honda_hq.jpg/1280px-Honda_hq.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Honda_hq.jpg/500px-Honda_hq.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The former headquarters in Minami-Aoyama, Minato, Tokyo, in use from 1985 to 2025. The building will be demolished to make room for a new building, scheduled for completion by the 2030 Japanese fiscal year.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHonda_hq.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Honda_T360_1963_in_Honda_Collection_Hall.jpg/500px-Honda_T360_1963_in_Honda_Collection_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Honda_T360_1963_in_Honda_Collection_Hall.jpg/1280px-Honda_T360_1963_in_Honda_Collection_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 